# Playwright output for the browser e2e lane
/tests/e2e/control-room/test-results/

# Fossil smoke-dir guard: the producer test now writes to os tmpdir
# (index-surface.test.ts), but a stale checkout could still litter here.
.project-configuration-smoke-*/

# --- Transitional Moe runtime scaffolding -----------------------------------
# Policy: docs/REPOSITORY_HYGIENE.md
#
# The repository-root `.moe/` directory mixes DURABLE project metadata with
# REGENERABLE daemon scaffolding. Durable records stay tracked and are never
# listed here: project.json, epics/, tasks/, channels/, messages/, roles/,
# agents/, skills/.
#
# This block is allow-by-omission: it names individual regenerable leaves and
# never uses a blanket `.moe/` or `.moe/**` rule. No moe-next source writes
# `.moe/` — the producer is the external transitional daemon — so a new leaf
# name cannot be predicted from this repo. Anything unlisted therefore stays
# visible to `git status` and defaults to tracked until a human classifies it.
# That fails closed: an unclassified durable record is noisy, never silently
# hidden.
#
# Every pattern is root-anchored with a leading `/` so it matches only the
# repository-root `.moe/` and never a fixture directory such as
# `packages/testkit/fixtures/**/.moe/`. Trailing `/` restricts a rule to
# directories. Forward slashes are Git-native and behave identically on
# Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# Ignoring a path does NOT untrack bytes already committed, and this block
# deletes nothing. See the policy document before removing any `.moe/` file.

# Daemon process state and lock
/.moe/daemon.json
/.moe/daemon.lock

# Activity log plus rotations. The generic `*.log` rule above catches
# `activity.log` only; rotated suffixes such as `activity.log.1` need this.
/.moe/activity.log
/.moe/activity.log.*

# Ephemeral fleet records, rebuilt by the daemon on restart
/.moe/workers/
/.moe/teams/
/.moe/proposals/
/.moe/sessions/

# Derived, debug, and scratch output
/.moe/cache/
/.moe/debug/
/.moe/tmp/
/.moe/scratch/

# moe-up dev launcher scratch state (stores, credentials) - never commit
.moe-dev/

# Activation store backups. `project.activate` measures a `backup` receipt by copying the
# store to <projectRoot>/.moe-next/backups/<stamp>.sqlite (activation-receipts-measure.ts),
# so activating from a checkout leaves multi-MB binaries in the working tree.
.moe-next/
